WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.550
Backup and recovery.

2
00:00:01.550 --> 00:00:04.662
The database and its
encryption key are a pair.

3
00:00:04.662 --> 00:00:07.700
Back up the database on
the FULL recovery model.

4
00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:12.712
Export the software key with the configuration
tool's key-export option, and keep

5
00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:17.425
it safe: CyberArk says that without it,
you cannot access data in the database.

6
00:00:17.425 --> 00:00:21.104
If an HSM holds the key,
use the HSM vendor's backup,

7
00:00:21.104 --> 00:00:25.794
and run the HSMs in high
availability, because if the HSM stays

8
00:00:25.794 --> 00:00:30.300
unreachable the platform retries,
logs, and then shuts down.

9
00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:33.912
CyberArk's disaster recovery
procedure has five steps.

10
00:00:33.912 --> 00:00:39.346
First, the prerequisites: local master
admin credentials, the database backup,

11
00:00:39.346 --> 00:00:44.026
the database connection details,
and the software key or HSM access.

12
00:00:44.026 --> 00:00:47.500
Second, stop the services
on every platform server.

13
00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:51.163
Third, restore the database
and recover its users.

14
00:00:51.163 --> 00:00:54.907
Fourth, re-enable SQL Service
Broker on the restored database,

15
00:00:54.907 --> 00:00:58.725
which is easy to forget and stops
the platform working if you do.

16
00:00:58.725 --> 00:01:02.995
Fifth, import the software key,
or reconnect the HSM through the

17
00:01:02.995 --> 00:01:07.512
Configuration Console or the
configuration tool's HSM PIN option.

18
00:01:07.512 --> 00:01:12.291
On the CA side, Microsoft recommends
backing up the CA with Backup-CARoleService

19
00:01:12.291 --> 00:01:14.359
before you change its permissions,

20
00:01:14.359 --> 00:01:17.425
which you're about to do for
the platform's CA account.

21
00:01:17.425 --> 00:01:21.873
The program's guidance is to rehearse
a full restore before Wave 2 exits,

22
00:01:21.873 --> 00:01:27.074
and the Federal Modernization Workbook's
Book 07 Chapter 08's rule applies to every

23
00:01:27.074 --> 00:01:32.200
key backup: store the backup and its
password through separate approved channels.

24
00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:37.380
Sources: CyberArk 26.1 Software
key backup; HSM configuration;

25
00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:42.459
Using HSM-protected keys;
Disaster recovery prerequisites,

26
00:01:42.459 --> 00:01:48.756
database recovery and HSM recovery;
System Requirements; Microsoft Learn,

27
00:01:48.756 --> 00:01:54.910
Secure, delegate and audit a certification
authority; Book 07, Chapter 08.
